From af2a41368d1aa6cf3cbb155d4c54e44f9cddd104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:32:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ssc): remove the gyro bias learned while the device
 holds still

Steam never applies its drift correction to the Steam Deck targets, so the
SSC's per-unit residual reaches games uncorrected (0.6 deg/s on an Odin 2
Portal, up to 3.6 deg/s on an Odin 3). Port GamepadMotionHelpers'
stillness calibration, whose thresholds adapt to each sensor's noise
floor, so the noisier QMI8658 in the Odin 3 calibrates too. It needs a
fresh accelerometer sample, restarts after a pause in the stream or a bad
sample, and skips all-zero reports.

New config.imu.gyro_auto_calibration option, off by default.

Assisted-by: LLM
